{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088308-explanation-required-mind-altering-legacy-attainments","id":1088308,"title":"Explanation required: Mind-altering Legacy Attainments.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-05T08:38:40-07:00","id":1088308,"title":"Explanation required: Mind-altering Legacy Attainments.","content":"So, i'm having some problems understanding some of the effects that Legacy Attainments have. Specifically, those associated with Mind. In the book explains clearly how the fire from a Forces-based Attainment is no different, once released, than any other fire. Therefore, it can be extinguished with magic, water, or whatever means we have at hand.<br /> <br /> Extrapolating it to Mind effects -for example, the Bearer's of the Eternal Voice memory warping Attainment-, how would it exactly work? I mean, one thing that changed from 1E is that now the effect does not automatically happens (it was kind of a Win Button movement; you could not fight it at all. It had just happened, BAM), there is a Clash of Wills to win. Ok.<br /> <br /> But how do you treat the Lasting effects? Are they something that fade with time? Are something permanent? (i suppose that if we have spent Reach enough on it, they could be). Can they be undone? I suppose with magic, or any other supernatural power... if you can win against the original Potency and Duration. Or maybe you don't have to fight against the original Attainment parameters? As they are simply... abilities, and after being affected by the Attainment these would be your new shiny memories, maybe the restoration intent should be treated as a normal spell, not a counterspell at all? <br /> <br /> And does a Bearer even care about the possibility of Withstanding? As i understand, there is no chance of Withstanding an Attainment effect, right?<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Oh well, i just realized i have a lot of somewhat stupid questions related to the Attainments. Let's see...<br /> <br /> - Can you made a Legacy Attainment out of a Arcana Attainment? Is that even worth? As we know, the Legacy Attainment can be always accesible -provided the user can spend mana and/or perform the actions, if there are such requirements-.<br /> <br /> - Are the Arcana Attainments allways &quot;on&quot;? For example, can a &quot;dead zone&quot;, as the one created by the Blasphemy spell (p. 171) effectively shut down the Arcana Attainments?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T08:50:49-07:00","id":1088315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088308-explanation-required-mind-altering-legacy-attainments#post1088308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, i'm having some problems understanding some of the effects that Legacy Attainments have. Specifically, those associated with Mind. In the book explains clearly how the fire from a Forces-based Attainment is no different, once released, than any other fire. Therefore, it can be extinguished with magic, water, or whatever means we have at hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have time to address your entire post, but you might clear some things up for yourself if I point out that the fire in the example is natural because the fire created from the spell that the attainment is based in is also natural. The fire isn't more mundane and natural because it comes from an attainment rather than spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T10:23:36-07:00","id":1088361,"title":"","content":"First of all, using Mind magic on someone else as a spell or an attainment doesn't provoke a CoW unless they have supernatural mental protection. Second of all yes, attainments have to deal with Withstand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T12:25:06-07:00","id":1088419,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the answers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T12:50:29-07:00","id":1088431,"title":"","content":"Attainment observed &quot;in motion&quot; is like looking at Stonehedge - it looks impossible and abnormal, and yet, it is. Just imagine that you are dealing with stonehedges of memories and other abnormal mental patterns instead of rocks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T14:47:13-07:00","id":1088499,"title":"","content":"As for Lasting, attainments can only be Lasting if the spell it's based on can be made Lasting. In cases of attainments with Duration as the primary factor you can get up to Indefinite though if that's where you put the attainment's dice penalties. to get it bumped up from the default Advanced Duration of a Year (When you're a Master). The effect of an attainment implanted Indefinite length memory would be that that's their memory, but like any memory it can be altered by Mind magic, mental powers, the passage of time, etc.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't be worth it to make a legacy attainment out of an arcana attainment. There would be no benefit since you get arcana attainments automatically upon achieving the requisite dot level in the arcana.<br /> <br /> Arcana attainments like any attainment are always available, they're not Supernal magic in and of themselves. They might be useless depending on your situation though, for instance in an Ansho casting magic is completely impossible so you also wouldn't be able to make use of the Matter 2 attainment to give Matter spells Advanced Duration for a point of mana. The Spirit Eyes ability would still work though, if you haven't been stripped of mana to power it yet.<br /> <br /> Blasphemy by the way doesn't prevent the use of spells or attainments, it destroys &quot;local&quot; supernatural energies with no direct effect on the powers of entities passing through its area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T01:51:32-07:00","id":1088664,"title":"","content":"Thank you, Mrmdubois, for that super-complete answer! All is clear now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}